course: dictionary
lesson: 8440
title: Feeling words: sadness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sadness is the feeling of being unhappy. People often feel it after losing something or someone, or when things go wrong. «The sadness after a death is called grief.» The sentence tells you that sadness is the feeling that comes after a loss.
explain: Sadness can be small or big. A small sadness may pass quickly, but a big, heavy sadness can last a long time. «Sadness that lasts many days and takes away the fun of things you loved» tells you this kind is heavy and does not go away quickly.
explain: Sadness is a normal feeling, and everyone has it. «Sadness is a normal feeling for everyone, boys and girls alike.» It can show as crying, being quiet or not wanting to play. Crying is a healthy way to let sadness out.
fact: Sadness is a noun, which means it is a name for a feeling.
fact: «Sadness» means the feeling of being unhappy, often after losing something or someone.
fact: Sadness can be small or big, and a big sadness can last a long time.
fact: Everyone feels sadness, and talking to a trusted adult, a friend or a pet can help.
fact: Useful phrases with «sadness» include «feel sadness», «full of sadness» and «happiness and sadness».
exercise: «The sadness after a death is called grief.» What does sadness mean in this sentence? | Being very tired after a long day | A game played with a ball | *The feeling of being unhappy after losing someone | A loud noise in the night
exercise: «Sadness that lasts many days can be a heavy feeling.» What does this tell you about sadness? | It is always over in one minute | *It can be big and heavy, and last a long time | It makes everyone laugh | It only happens to grown-ups
exercise: Ayesha says sadness is only for babies. Is she right? | Sadness never happens to children | Yes, but only girls feel it | *No, sadness is normal for everyone, boys and girls alike | Yes, only babies feel sad
test: What is a healthy way to let sadness out? | Holding it in until it goes away | Shouting at the walls | Hiding from everyone for ever | *Crying
test: «Sadness that lasts many days and takes away the fun of things you loved» should be told to whom? | The television | Nobody, keep it secret | *A parent, teacher or doctor | Your pet only
exam: Which phrase best shows sadness as a big, heavy feeling? | A quick laugh | *A heavy sadness that lasts for weeks | A happy song | A small tickle
